# acceptance-mutation-manifest-end

# Spec §5 and §6.2 (Edit). The status is derived from the definition and the
# completions, so editing can change the status and the place in
# Pendientes. Editing does not touch the completions or creadaEn.
#   Relative: V = U + new interval.
#   Calendar: N = the first occurrence of the new rule after the saved P,
#     even if P is no longer an occurrence of the new rule.
#   P = the greater of the ocurrenciaCubierta values and the days of completadoEn of
#     the completions without ocurrenciaCubierta (done when the task was
#     relative or one-off); with no completions, the day before creadaEn.
#   Waiting start = the most recent completadoEn or, if there is none, creadaEn.
#   A task with completions that becomes one-off leaves Pendientes (§5.1).
# Dates and times in local time; progress is a fraction between 0 and 1,
# compared exactly. Reference week: Monday 2026-07-13 to Sunday
# 2026-07-19. Each scenario picks values for which, without the edit, the
# result would be different (except where the comment says otherwise).
# "has a completion that covers ..." is an already stored completion; when
# the step gives no time for it, that time does not affect the result.
Feature: Status after editing

  # Status after editing 1
  # Recurring relative: shortening the interval leaves it pending (before, waiting).
  Scenario Outline: Status after editing 1
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the task was completed on <completed>
    When I edit the task to relative recurring every <every_new> <unit_new>
    And I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is pendiente

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | completed           | every_new  | unit_new     | now                 |
      | 3    | dias   | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 1          | dias         | 2026-07-16T10:00:00 |
      | 12   | horas  | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 4          | horas        | 2026-07-15T12:30:00 |

  # Status after editing 2
  # Recurring relative: lengthening the interval leaves it waiting, with the progress of
  # the new interval (before, overdue or pending).
  Scenario Outline: Status after editing 2
    Given a relative recurring task every <every> <unit>
    And the task was completed on <completed>
    When I edit the task to relative recurring every <every_new> <unit_new>
    And I query the status on <now>
    Then the status is en espera
    And the progress is <progress>

    Examples:
      | every | unit   | completed           | every_new  | unit_new     | now                 | progress |
      | 4    | horas  | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 2          | dias         | 2026-07-15T20:00:00 | 0.25     |
      | 1    | dias   | 2026-07-15T08:00:00 | 36         | horas        | 2026-07-16T11:00:00 | 0.75     |

